</div>

<div class="banner">
    <strong>Confirmed architecture:</strong> ASP.NET Core becomes live primary; PHP stays installed as <strong>reference</strong> so you can still see previous results and spot gaps.
    Status: <code>@phpRef.Status</code>. Locks: <code>cutoverAllowed=@phpRef.CutoverAllowed.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()</code>,
    <code>readyForPhpRemoval=@phpRef.ReadyForPhpRemoval.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()</code>,
    <code>RequirePhpFallback=@phpRef.RequirePhpFallback.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()</code>.
    Tenant hosts keep PHP chrome until unlocked parity shadows.
    Path: <a href="/migration/aspnet-zero-php-path">/migration/aspnet-zero-php-path</a> ·
    <a href="/migration/php-reference-mode">/migration/php-reference-mode</a>.
</div>

